Let venus import a shm resource as host-pointer memory.

With the host-pointer patch, host-visible memory on a driver that exports no fd
is shared shm, and its blob is a VIRGL_RESOURCE_FD_SHM resource. Another
context that attaches the blob and imports it with
VkImportMemoryResourceInfoMESA was refused: the import path translates a
resource into VkImportMemoryFdInfoKHR and knows only dma-buf and opaque fds.

On Tessera that context is the display server, importing an application's
frame. The guest allocates memory asynchronously, so it never saw the
VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE, and the vkBindImageMemory2 that followed named
memory the host had never made: "failed to look up object 99 of type 8", a CS
error, and a dead ring that aborted the display server.

A shm resource now keeps a descriptor for its pages. vkAllocateMemory importing
one maps the pages again from it and imports the pointer through
VK_EXT_external_memory_host when the driver offers that. Mapping them again
rather than reusing the resource's mapping keeps the driver's buffer valid if
the resource is detached first. The memory keeps the descriptor too, so it can
be exported in turn.

The blob of a host-pointer VkDeviceMemory, in the context that made it, was
also stored as a shm resource with -1 written into the fd half of its union and
garbage left in the pointer half, which the resource's free then unmapped. A
shm resource now always stores its pointer, NULL included.

Applies after the venus-host-pointer patch.

